  "title": "A novel self-correcting direct position determination in asynchronous sensor networks",
  "abstractNote": "This paper presents a novel self-calibration direct position determination (SC-DPD) method in asynchronous sensor networks without the aid of anchor sources. By leveraging the consistency of asynchronous clock bias across different intercepted signal batches, the localization cost function is derived to effectively mitigate asynchronous effects. Simulation results demonstrate enhanced performance of the proposed method over existing studies: (1) superior localization accuracy, particularly in low Signal-to-Noise Ratio (SNR) conditions, (2) lower system complexity through anchor-free operation, (3) reduced computational complexity without clock bias estimation in the asynchronous sensor networks. The proposed method bridges the gap between theoretical DPD frameworks and practical deployment constraints, particularly for large-scale sensor networks.",
